# IoT-Based Industrial Plant Safety Gas Leakage System

## Overview

The IoT-Based Industrial Plant Safety Gas Leakage System is designed to detect hazardous gas leakages in industrial environments and provide real-time monitoring and alerts. The system uses ESP8266 NodeMCU and MQ-series gas sensors to detect gases such as LPG, Methane, and Benzene.

Sensor data is transmitted over Wi-Fi to the Blynk platform, allowing remote monitoring through a mobile application. When gas levels exceed predefined safety limits, the system activates a buzzer alert and updates the cloud dashboard.

## Features

* Real-time gas monitoring
* LPG, Methane, and Benzene detection
* Wi-Fi enabled cloud connectivity
* Blynk dashboard integration
* Buzzer-based alert system
* Continuous environmental monitoring
* Low-cost and scalable industrial safety solution

## Hardware Components

* ESP8266 NodeMCU
* MQ-4 Gas Sensor
* MQ-6 Gas Sensor
* MQ-135 Gas Sensor
* Buzzer
* LCD Display
* LEDs
* Power Supply Unit

## Software Used

* Arduino IDE
* Embedded C
* Blynk IoT Platform

## Working Principle

1. Gas sensors continuously monitor the surrounding environment.
2. NodeMCU reads sensor values and processes the data.
3. Gas concentration levels are transmitted to the Blynk cloud platform through Wi-Fi.
4. If gas levels exceed safety thresholds:

   * Buzzer alert is activated.
   * Gas status is updated on the Blynk dashboard.
5. If gas levels remain within limits, the system continues monitoring.

## Technologies Used

* Embedded C
* Internet of Things (IoT)
* ESP8266
* Wi-Fi Communication
* Cloud Monitoring
* Sensor Networks

## Applications

